s unit that runs National  University as well as National Sister  colleges he got a start in business in  the printing industry when he opened  Cunningham Graphics International which  is a company that printed analystic  research reports in the year 2000 he  sold the company to automatic data  processing for 136 million and he went  back to school for his PhD and has  worked in higher education ever since  under Cunningham's leadership National  has grown from about 33 000 students to  forty five thousand he's also LED their  transition from a hybrid online  in-person model to primarily online  which has really helped National out  during the pandemic since the university  already had the digital learning  infrastructure it needed to quickly  pivot to online meanwhile most colleges  and universities were just creating or  scaling up their digital offerings and  National already had it in place impact  without scale is good but it's not great  what we want to do is have impact with  scale number one it creates so many more  opportunities for students around the  world and it transforms Society because  if you change one person's life you  change their life forever if you change  thousands of people's lives forever you  change society for the better forever  and unfortunately uh there's a hard  truth the cost of acquisition of student  acquisition is very expensive  so what we want to do when we're doing  right now is creating economy of scale  so that we reduce the cost by growing  the organization so the cost to our  students goes down our goal is to  continually reduce pricing this last  year we reduced our net tuition prices  by over 20 percent  Michael is an academic  which is  which he's also not been afraid to make  some controversial decisions either  including changing programs and cunning  faculty which is typically met with a  lot of pushback and not every leader can  follow through on it if you think about  it we're we're experiencing a period of  punctuated equilibrium and basically  what it means is when when you have an  equilibrium in any business or in any  Enterprise or Society for that matter  and things are at steady state and then  something jolts that steady state and  changes things that creates a lot of  hardship but it also creates opportunity  so previously in my business we were  Printing and then Distributing but with  digital technology we were able to  distribute electronically first around  the world and then print locally  So It sped up our our response time from  four days around the world to one day  and it brought the cost down by 25 so  what we're happening right now if you  think about it the same digital paradigm  shift is happening throughout society  and then on top of that we had the  pandemic  and then overnight whole society was  jolted and and people were working  remotely people were learning remotely  trying to figure it out and we were in a  position because we've been doing it  online for a long time education online  we were one of the first movers in the  space we were able to use that  opportunity to expand our business  expand our footprint and expand the  value of our proposition to students not  only our existing students but uh new  entrance to the marketplace
 

